.TH DDNSD 8 "October 2026" "ddnsd 0.0.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
ddnsd \- dynamic DNS daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ddnsd
.RB [ \-c
.IR config ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ddnsd
periodically finds this host's public IPv4 and IPv6 addresses and keeps the
A and AAAA records of a domain pointed at them, using the Cloudflare or No-IP
DNS provider.
.PP
Addresses are found with HTTP echo services (icanhazip, ipify or custom URLs)
or from the global addresses of local network interfaces, tried in the
configured order for each address family.
.PP
The daemon exits when the provider rejects an update in a way that needs the
configuration to be fixed, such as invalid credentials, and waits as long as
the provider asks after server errors.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIconfig\fR
Read the configuration from
.IR config .
The default is
.IR /etc/ddnsd.yaml .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ddnsd.yaml
The YAML configuration file. It contains provider credentials and must not be
readable by group or others, e.g. mode 0600.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/ddnsd/examples/ddnsd.example.yaml
An example configuration describing all settings.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter, e.g.
.B debug
or
.BR ddnsd=debug ;
the default is
.BR info .
.SH EXAMPLES
Configure and start the service:
.PP
.nf
.RS
install \-m 600 /usr/share/doc/ddnsd/examples/ddnsd.example.yaml /etc/ddnsd.yaml
editor /etc/ddnsd.yaml
systemctl start ddnsd
.RE
.fi
